WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.440
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.580
Now that the award-winning Red Zone Recovery Plan has been

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:18.840
signed off by government, we can begin the
work.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.910
What was formerly known as red zone, is
now an area of regeneration.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.700
The consultation that has taken place has
been widely acclaimed, winning the supreme

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.480
awards at both the New Zealand Planning Institute
awards and the Local Government Management Awards

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.220
Design work for the roading, recreational
facilities, and greenspaces featured in the

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.560
plan are the key priorities.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.490
The waterfront is already looking amazing
and our community will continue to drive the

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:47.860
process in partnership with the Council through
every stage of the development.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.980
This month, we’re looking at the timeline
for completion of the various projects within

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.080
the Regeneration areas.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:02.720
The job is massive, covering five areas - over
100 hectares combined.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.720
Most of the work is expected to be finished
in the next two to ten years.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.540
The first work to begin will be roading and
we’ve been receiving feedback from our community

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:15.980
about the roading designs for Courtenay Drive
and the new roading link between Feldwick

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.460
Drive, Bracebridge Street and Cass Street.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.840
We consulted with the community recently on the design for the rebuild of Courtenay Drive

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.260
and hopefully we'll have contractors on site in July and the work all finished by the end of the year.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:34.160
In 2018, design work for the sports fields
will be underway and construction of the Riverview

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.940
Terraces will be progressing.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.580
Work will also begin on the new roading link
in Kaiapoi East regeneration area, and we

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:44.530
should see the first sod being turned for
the BMX track and dog park.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.540
Well the planning and design of the new reserves and parks is well underway, and we’re working on some

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.310
really exciting features.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.660
We’re looking forward to sharing these ideas with the community over the coming months.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.140
Also planned for this area are a food forest
and walking and cycling tracks.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:01.780
These are all activities that our community told
us they wanted during the development of the

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.840
draft Recovery Plan.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.729
Land is also being set aside for a motorhome
and caravan park and for exciting new retail

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.300
and business options for the Kaiapoi Town
Centre.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.290
So this is an exciting time for Kaiapoi, and
we want you to be a part of it.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.169
The Kaiapoi- Tuahiwi Community Board will be holding
fortnightly drop-in sessions here at the library

00:02:22.169 --> 00:02:27.480
in the Ruataniwha civic centre and we'd like you to come in and talk to us.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:34.340
Next month, we’ll be looking at the design
for the Riverview Terraces on the north side

00:02:34.359 --> 00:02:38.370
of the Kaiapoi River and talk to local developer,
Jedd Pearce.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.639
We’ll meet landscape architect Kevin Dwyer
and check in on what progress has been made

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.960
along the Kaiapoi River waterfront.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:56.220
For more information about the regeneration,
visit any council service centre or waimakariri.govt.nz/regeneration.

